# Served by Cloudflare's static asset handler.
#
# @astrojs/sitemap emits a sitemap *index* (sitemap-index.xml) pointing at one urlset, which
# is a valid top-level sitemap and is what robots.txt names — discovery works without this
# line. It is here for the two cases robots.txt does not cover: a crawler that probes
# /sitemap.xml by convention, and a person who tries the address the main site uses, since
# orator.space serves /sitemap.xml and two hostnames disagreeing about the name of the same
# thing is a paper cut with no upside.
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap-index.xml  301
